:: Nursery encounter - burned out [bg-nursery]
<h1 class="ptitle">NURSERY</h1>
<br /><br />
/* A caretaker is losing the fight with the workload. Odds come from the same numbers as burning out overnight. */
<<set _enc = setup.nurseryEncounters>>
<<set _cast = _enc.cast()>>
<<if !_cast>>
	<<goto 'Nursery'>>
<<else>>
<<set _carer = _cast.carer>>
<<set _name = setup.displayName(_carer)>>
<<set _heOrShe = setup.pronounceWhat(_carer)>>
<<set _hisOrHer = setup.pronounceWhos(_carer)>>
<<set _himOrHer = setup.pronounceWho(_carer)>>

The noise reaches you first. Two children are fighting over a blanket, one is crying for no reason anyone can find, and a bunch of toys are scattered on the floor. <<=_name>> is in the middle of the room with a basket of washing on one hip and a toddler on the other, turning from one problem to the next without getting to any of them.
<br /><br />
<<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> sees you and tries to pull <<=_himOrHer>>self together. It doesn't quite work. <<=ucfirst(_hisOrHer)>> eyes are red, and <<=_hisOrHer>> voice is thin.
<br /><br />
<<sayNpc _carer>>
	I've got it. I'm fine. I just need a minute, and there aren't any, and every time I fix one thing... I'm sorry. It's fine. I've got it.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />

<div id="nce_choices">
	<<link 'Roll up your sleeves and help (Uses 1 hour)'>>
		<<replace '#nce_choices'>>
			<<addmins 60>>
			<<run _enc.change(_carer, 'relationship', 4, 6)>>
			<<run setup.nurseryBehavior.change(5, 10)>>
			You take the basket out of <<=_hisOrHer>> hands, gather up the scattered toys, and tell the blanket fighters that they now each have half a chore. For the next hour you do whatever is in front of you. It isn't glamorous, and you get kicked once, but the room slowly comes back under control.
			<br /><br />
			<<=_name>> eventually sits down on the edge of a cot and puts <<=_hisOrHer>> face in <<=_hisOrHer>> hands for a moment. When <<=_heOrShe>> looks up, <<=_heOrShe>> is almost smiling.
			<br /><br />
			<<sayNpc _carer>>
				Nobody's ever done that before. Just come in and helped. I won't forget it.
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			[[Continue|Nursery]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
	<<link `'Berate ' + _himOrHer + ' for letting things get out of control'`>>
		<<replace '#nce_choices'>>
			<<run _enc.change(_carer, 'sub', 5, 8)>>
			<<run _enc.change(_carer, 'happy', -10, -5)>>
			<<run setup.nurseryBehavior.change(3, 5)>>
			You tell <<=_himOrHer>>, in front of everyone, that this is exactly what <<=_heOrShe>> is here to prevent, and that you expect better. The room goes quiet. The two children drop the blanket, and even the crying stops.
			<br /><br />
			<<=_name>> stands very still until you have finished, and then nods with <<=_hisOrHer>> eyes on the floor.
			<br /><br />
			<<sayNpc _carer>>
				Yes. You're right. I'm sorry. It won't happen again.
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			The children give <<=_himOrHer>> no trouble for the rest of the shift. <<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> doesn't look at you again before you go.
			<br /><br />
			[[Continue|Nursery]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
	<<link 'Do nothing'>>
		<<replace '#nce_choices'>>
			<<run _enc.change(_carer, 'happy', -6, -4)>>
			<<run setup.nurseryBehavior.change(-5, -3)>>
			You tell yourself <<=_heOrShe>> said <<=_heOrShe>> has it, and you go on about your business. Behind you, the noise picks up again. You can hear <<=_name>>'s voice over the top of it for a while, and then you can't.
			<br /><br />
			[[Continue|Nursery]]
			<<nurseryEffects>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
</div>
<</if>>
